# Amendment #57 — workspace-sync resolver cost overhaul (Bundle α)

2026-04-26. Follow-on to amendment #56 (workspace-sync, sealed at
`0607dc7`). The milestone live-test against pos3 (2026-04-27)
halted on a `claude -p` 120s subprocess timeout at conflict 3 of
46. The 2 verdicts produced before halt were sharp (0.88
confidence, amendment-aware reasoning); the failure was cost,
not correctness.

Bundle α attacks resolver cost from three independent angles in
one amendment, each compositional with the others:

  - **α.1 (AC.WSα.1, AC.WSα.2)** — Content-vs-canonical-history
    ancestor detection. Before invoking the resolver, walk
    canonical's git history (`git log --all --follow -- <path>`)
    looking for an ancestor commit whose blob for the conflicted
    path matches the workspace's `installed_sha256` byte-for-
    byte. When found, fast-path resolve as
    `inferred-accept-canonical` with confidence 1.0 — the
    workspace didn't diverge, it's just behind. Per-conflict
    cache (`<workspace>/.pos/sync/<ref>/ancestor-cache.yaml`,
    keyed by `(path, workspace_sha256)`) avoids re-walks across
    re-runs. Depth cap 200 (workspace-tunable; D-1 LOCKED).
    Empirical 97.8% skip rate against pos3's 46-conflict audit
    per the NN-skippability research note.

  - **α.2 (AC.WSα.3 through AC.WSα.6)** — Deterministic-merge
    with LLM-verify-gate. Replaces the slow LLM-as-generator
    path (full-file output, 60-120s wall-time) with a
    four-step classifier+deterministic+verifier pipeline:
    (a) classify (~50 token output) tags the file's
    structural class (`append-only-list` / `log` /
    `tracker-table` / `free-prose` / `unknown`);
    (b) deterministic merge primitive runs in ~0.01s, free,
    audit-grade reproducible;
    (c) verify (~200 token output) reads the deterministic
    result against both inputs + the named class + the
    primitive's trace, asks "is this actually structurally a
    {class}?" as the FIRST verification step (Hard Constraint
    #8 binding); a `class_mismatch=true` flag forces
    `passed=false` via Pydantic model_validator (rubber-stamp
    prevention);
    (d) apply or fall back: verify passes → accept verdict
    with `INFERRED_MERGED`; verify fails OR classifier returns
    `unknown` OR primitive raises `PrimitiveDeclined` → fall
    back to today's full LLM-generator path (preserves the
    correctness ceiling — AC.WSα.6).
    Generalises FUTURE_IDEAS Idea 20 (LLM-as-classifier +
    LLM-as-verifier, never LLM-as-generator).

  - **α.3 (AC.WSα.8)** — MCP-isolated subprocess. The
    `claude -p` subprocess invocation in `_resolver_client.py`
    now appends `--strict-mcp-config --mcp-config <empty>` so
    the subprocess does NOT load the parent session's MCP
    servers (preventing bun-process contention with telegram
    MCP, memory-graphiti MCP, etc.). Empty MCP config
    (`{"mcpServers": {}}`) written once at
    `_ClaudePrintResolverClient.__init__` to a process-cached
    tempfile path; every invoke appends the flags
    referencing it. OAuth/Claude-Max auth path preserved (no
    env-scrubber changes; no `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` requirement).
    D-3 RE-LOCKED 2026-04-27 — initial scope as
    `--bare`-for-cold-start was reframed to MCP-isolation
    after empirical verification under Claude Max OAuth.

  - **AC.WSα.7** — observability spans for each new step
    (`pos.sync.merge_gate.ancestor_check`,
    `pos.sync.merge_gate.classify`,
    `pos.sync.merge_gate.verify`) emitted via the existing
    `pos.workspace_sync` tracer. observability-aggregator
    ingests for free.

